GUI-Tkinter
-Tkinter is a in built python library
-we can use it py importing it
=import tkinter

#Tk()
-it is used to create an window object
-window object is where user interact
Syntax:
window=tkinter.Tk()

#mainloop()
-after creating window mainloop() will present windows continuously
Syntax:
window.mainloop()

#title()
-to change the title or name of window using window object
syntax:window.title("name of title")

#Label()
-to add text inside the window
syntax:
label=tk.Label(text="hello")

#pack()
-using pack() we can bring text or button on window inside pack() we can change the side of text left,right,button,expand=True for center
 pack(side=any side)
-label.pack()

*using label and pack() method the window automatically take the size of window as required but to keep minimum default size
 we use minsize()

#minsize()
syntax:window.minsize(width=,height=)


*to change the font of text in window we can change it in Label() method or using font class
syntax:label=tk.Label(text="hello",font=("Times New Roman",20,"bold")

*font.Font()
-first import tkinter.font as font
syntax:
custom_font=tk.font.Font(family="time new roman",size=13,slant="italic")
-we can now use custom_font in label()

!!above codes are on p1.py

#after creation label we can change the text
1.label["text"]="have a nice day"
2.label.config(text="have a nice day")

*in label.config we can change any property of label

#Button
-a clickable button
-to make an use of button use command=function name

-def butt():
  label.config(text="thank you")

syntax:
button=tk.Button(text="click here",command=butt)
button.pack()

!!above code are on p2.py

#Entry()
-user enters an text in window or take user input
syntax:
user_input=tk.Entry() *inside entry we can change the width and height or set it

*to make user_input mask or password or to hide
syntax:
user_input=tk.Entry(show="*")

*to make used of or fetch user input
#get()
syntax:
user_input.get()

!!above code are at P3.py

#ttk
-import it first:form tkinter import ttk
-improve module or Tk()/better version

#quitting the window
-syntax:window.destroy

!!! above code in P4.py

